WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:00.610
Thank you.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.880
Every man is an imperfection, fatal weakness, seed of destruction.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.040
You discovered that, Foster, when you traded principles for personal glory,

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.200
sacrificed integrity for power.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.980
You discovered that in eight short months.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.540
...climbing to a governor's mansion from a district attorney's office.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:42.570
Hello, Jack. He's in conference. Can I take a message?

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:43.360
Hello, Mary.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:43.920
Hello.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.630
The Beckhurst file for the bar.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.560
He's in conference.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.260
Well, can I trust you with it?

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.140
Take him in.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.820
Well, I guess so.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.080
It is personal. You're not an old maid, are you?

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.360
The Beckhurst file, Mr. Foster.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.120
Thanks, Wolf. I don't suppose there's any secret about it. I'll be 48 next month.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.060
48? That's just about right.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:06.900
I'll be old.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.500
Right for what?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.720
Gossip around Governor Lambert's going to retire. He's old.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.850
In 70. The race will be wide open this fall.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:21.780
Very interesting.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.250
Thought it might be.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.520
I got some more gossip for you, too. A fellow of 48 could win.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.540
With the right sponsors.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.960
Provided the sponsors are out of jail.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.090
They will be.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.750
That's not the way the jury's going to feel about your man, Hanson.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:41.140
I think it is, after what I heard today.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.460
Seems you had a subpoena issued for some books of his.

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:46.970
Books with figures in them.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:48.690
Go on.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.700
Hanson was going to bring them down like you wanted.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.120
Only something funny happened this morning.

00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:54.160
They caught fire.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.400
I don't believe you.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:56.420
Yes.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.350
I'd have brought them myself to show you, only...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.590
I didn't think you'd want your office cluttered up with ashes.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:04.920
You licked Foster.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.150
No, and you don't think so either.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.920
You wouldn't be talking about governorships.

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:10.950
I'll tell you about it.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:13.460
My people up here have been complaining about you.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.920
Breaking their slot machines, closing the bookies,

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.520
ranking off the numbers game.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.920
It's cost them and me a lot of money.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.780
Then Hanson, you missed, but I have an idea you'll try again.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:27.180
Of course, there's another way to stop you, but that's messy.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.260
Blood, a lot of bad publicity.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:29.980
I don't think...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.900
I don't think either of us care for that.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:34.090
I gather you're offering me a choice.

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:36.780
A governorship or a shroud.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.650
I don't want to put it anyway.

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:50.090
Suppose you get out. You don't want to dance, eh?

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.320
That's right. Maybe you will anyway.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.220
Reverend Dr. Garfield. Come in, Tom.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:01.410
Trouble with Faulkner?

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:02.810
Yes, bad trouble.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.720
He and his man, Hanson, have outsmarted me.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.340
Sit down, Tom.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.230
How, Joseph?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.770
Burnt Hanson's records.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.580
But you must have expected that.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.620
No, not the way I had the thing set up.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.160
Of course I wanted the records,

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.580
but I knew if I went after them before the trial, he'd destroy them.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.840
So I built my case to look as though I wasn't going to use them at all,

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.810
figuring on a raid later on when he was off guard.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.930
One of my assistants secured the subpoena this morning,

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.120
but got two to Hanson, too.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.920
Oh, I wouldn't worry. You made a fine...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.490
record. No district attorney in the country's done better. That's not me. It's the little people,

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:40.770
the corner grocer, the basement tailor, and the one truck cleaner. All paying from five to ten

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:46.890
dollars a week for protection. From what? Hanson. Someday he'll overreach him. Someday's not soon

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:52.790
enough. I'm going to get him, and I'm going to get him now if I happen. I'm sorry. Why should I be

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:59.520
bothering you with my troubles? Did you bring the boy? Wolf has him outside. Has him? He's a bit wild.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:01.940
That's why we have the club.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.410
I'm Adelie.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:15.850
What are you going to do, make me a boy scout?

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.070
You know what I'd do with you.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.050
You ain't big enough.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:18.750
Come with me, Larry.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:19.840
St. Joseph.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:20.200
Yes?

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.760
Wouldn't the burning of the books be evidence of Hanson's guilt?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.920
Would if I could prove he did it, which I can't.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.280
Pity, for all the work you've done.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:29.140
Well, let's call the office, Larry.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:29.740
What for?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:30.810
I just want to talk with you.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.610
The kid was mine.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:34.550
He wouldn't be here.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:38.140
Yeah.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:40.960
Sooner stand.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:43.730
What have they got you for, Larry?

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:45.250
Out of rep.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:47.350
Tell me about it.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:48.680
Why should I?

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.430
No reason, except that I was once in the same spot.

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.150
Don't give me that soap.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:55.260
When you were a kid, you wore lace pants.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.780
Listen, when I was your age, I could lick every kid in the waterfront and most of the

00:05:59.780 --> 00:05:59.960
sale.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:03.560
too. Laced pants. But I'll tell you

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:06.560
something, Larry. I found out it doesn't pay.

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.500
Not in the long run. Not anymore than what you're doing.

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:11.030
Do you know if it weren't for Dr. Garfield

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.550
you'd be in a reform school? What's the matter with

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.490
reform school? You want to go there? Sure.

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.740
This is sissy stuff. The guys in the

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.880
block would laugh at me. Do you think anybody laughs

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.080
at me? No. Well, there.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.690
Why don't you give it a try? Say for a month.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.420
No. I don't think I'd...

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.520
Are you ready to come home, darling?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.780
I'm always ready to come home.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.420
Martha, this is Larry Price.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.560
He's thinking of joining us.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:36.720
Oh, you'll like it here, Larry.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:38.190
Maybe.

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.040
You look tired, dear.

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:40.560
A bad day.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:41.320
Not good.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.040
Hanson?

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:43.500
I'm afraid he's out for new with me.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:44.480
Oh, what a shame.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:47.280
Joseph would rather convict Hanson than be president, I think.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.500
He's the last of our evil forces.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.720
He's the last and the biggest.

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:53.510
He's like an octopus, sucking the blood of every little business in the city.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.970
You know, I'd give my soul to nail him.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:58.360
Mr. Foster?

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.040
Yes?

00:06:59.220 --> 00:06:59.980
What is it, sir?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.890
You told me to give this to you.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:07.550
Thanks. Listen to this.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:12.480
If you want to nail Hanson, drop around to the China coast at 8 tonight.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:13.960
Well, it's almost as if he heard you.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:14.580
Son!

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:15.500
He beat it.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:18.910
Joseph, you're not thinking of going.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.210
What if I knew where he was?

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:23.070
There's a joint on Front Street, next to the M&R Wharf.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:23.730
Thanks.

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:26.710
Now, Martha, I'm perfectly capable of taking care of myself.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.860
I'll run you home, and then I'll drop in on my anonymous friend.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:31.030
Probably just a joke.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:32.660
Bye, Tom.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:33.240
Bye, Joseph.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.570
Well, Larry, will you give us a try?

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.490
Yeah, I guess so.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.250
I've had a tough trip, Joe.

00:08:35.570 --> 00:08:39.610
Yeah, two days out, the motor countdown and the radio.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:41.370
For a week, we drift sound.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:48.810
Gentlemen, where'd you come from?

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:49.700
Out there.

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:51.350
Nothing but bay out there.

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:52.050
That's right.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.980
Like drinks, separate drinks brought to this table, some ginger ale.

